{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_kuberneteslease", "label": "KubernetesLease", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "Implements Lease against the coordination.k8s.io/v1 Lease resource; the API server's etcd-backed store gives the single-holder guarantee regardless of pod scheduling or partitions between pods.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_kubernetesleaseoptions", "label": "KubernetesLeaseOptions", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_credential_triple", "label": "apiServerUrl, authToken and caCert are one credential", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "They are all-or-nothing because per-field fallback to the in-cluster mount sent the pod's own ServiceAccount token to a host it was not issued for; a partial set throws OptionsError, and the URL must be https since the client dials node:https regardless.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_required_fields", "label": "Required fields enforced at construction", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Without owner the Lease is written with no spec.holderIdentity and an unowned lease reads as free to every pod \u2014 every acquire returns true and the single-holder guarantee is gone without one logged error; a missing ttlMs reaches the same outcome via a NaN expiry.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_stale_holder_tolerance", "label": "Stale-holder fields are never taken at face value", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "leaseDurationSeconds and renewTime were written by the holder being judged, so duration counts for at most 4x the challenger's own ttlMs (generous so a rolling TTL raise does not let an old node evict a live holder), a renewTime more than one ttlMs ahead counts as expired, and a missing or unparseable one counts as live. A corrupt record costs at most 4x ttlMs of unavailability instead of pinning the lease forever.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_acquire_flow", "label": "Acquire flow", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "GET, then CREATE if absent, else check holder and renewTime; atomicity comes from K8s optimistic concurrency via resourceVersion, so two simultaneous claims on a stale lease produce one winner.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_renewal_loop", "label": "Renewal via resourceVersion CAS", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Renewal re-PUTs the whole object with the last-read resourceVersion, turning the write into a compare-and-set; there is no retry budget in the loop, so any failure \u2014 transient, 409 or 404 \u2014 fires onLost immediately.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_rbac_role", "label": "Lease RBAC Role", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Without get/create/update/patch/delete on leases, acquire rejects with 403; without delete, release works but leaves the object behind harmlessly.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_loss_detection", "label": "Loss detection", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "onLost fires on a renewal CAS conflict, on observing an external modification, or when a partition prevents renewal for longer than ttlMs.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_kuberneteslease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_kubernetesleaseoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_credential_triple", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_kubernetesleaseoptions", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_required_fields", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_kubernetes_lease_kubernetesleaseoptions", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/kubernetes-lease.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_s